# Kconfig — application tunables for the clamp-on thermal leak sensor.
#
# Every number the firmware behaviour depends on lives here rather than as a
# literal in a .c file, for one specific reason: the P1 field trial
# (08-roadmap.md §3, "P1 — Prove the alert") is a parameter sweep. The
# nuisance-alert rate is the gate, the dwell window is the main knob, and a knob
# you have to recompile a source file to turn does not get turned.
#
# The pure-logic modules (leak_detect.c, uplink.c, valve.c, install_probe.c) do
# NOT read these symbols. main() copies them into the *_cfg structs those
# modules take as arguments, which is what keeps those four files free of any
# build-system dependency and host-testable. Do not add a CONFIG_ reference to
# any of them.

mainmenu "Clamp-on thermal water-leak sensor"

menu "Leak sensor application"

config APP_SAMPLE_PERIOD_S
	int "Sensor sample period, seconds"
	default 60
	range 10 900
	help
	  How often the two TMP117s are read and the detector is run. This is
	  deliberately much faster than the uplink heartbeat: the detection
	  decision is local (04-connectivity.md §4.2) so it must not be limited to
	  the radio's cadence, and a 15-minute detector could not resolve a dwell
	  window at all.

config APP_HEARTBEAT_MIN
	int "Default uplink heartbeat, minutes"
	default 15
	range 1 240
	help
	  Default only. The backend can change it at runtime within
	  contracts/INTERFACES.md §2's 1..240 via the set_heartbeat downlink, and
	  the new value is persisted to NVS. 15 minutes is the figure the
	  connectivity analysis uses when it computes the worst-case cloud-shutoff
	  latency that justifies deciding locally.

config APP_MIN_UPLINK_INTERVAL_S
	int "Minimum spacing between non-heartbeat uplinks, seconds"
	default 300
	range 30 3600
	help
	  Rate limit on threshold frames. A verdict oscillating around a threshold
	  must not become a transmit storm: on a primary cell that is a battery
	  fault, and on a shared gateway it is somebody else's outage.

config APP_LEAK_DWELL_S
	int "Leak dwell window, seconds"
	default 1800
	range 60 14400
	help
	  How long a negative delta excursion must persist before it is called
	  leak_suspected. THE nuisance-rate knob, and the thing the P1 gate
	  (<0.5 nuisance alerts/device-year) is actually measuring. The default is
	  30 minutes: longer than the longest ordinary draw-off in the simulator's
	  scenario set (shower_morning, appliance_use) and much shorter than the
	  hours a slow leak takes to become expensive.

config APP_LEAK_EXCURSION_CC
	int "Excursion threshold below baseline, centi-degrees C"
	default 150
	range 20 2000
	help
	  How far below the learned per-device baseline the delta must fall to open
	  an excursion. Not a global temperature threshold: the baseline adapts per
	  device because housing stock varies (contracts/INTERFACES.md §5
	  behaviour 5).

config APP_FREEZE_CC
	int "Freeze-risk threshold, centi-degrees C"
	default 400
	range -1000 1500
	help
	  Pipe temperature at or below which the detector reports freeze_risk and
	  the uplink sets the cold_warning flag. One threshold drives both so that
	  the wire flag and the local verdict can never disagree. Application A4 —
	  free upside on the same sensor.

config APP_INSTALL_PROBE_SAMPLES
	int "Install probe duration, 1 Hz samples"
	default 60
	range 20 300
	help
	  How long the install verification watches the two channels while the
	  installer runs the nearest fixture. Install-verification telemetry is a
	  hard product requirement (08-roadmap.md P1, §8 risk 4), and 60 s is about
	  as long as an installer will actually hold a tap open.

config APP_BLE_WINDOW_S
	int "BLE commissioning/recovery advertising window, seconds"
	default 600
	range 30 3600
	depends on BT
	help
	  How long connectable advertising stays up after boot or after a press of
	  the recovery reed switch. Time-boxed rather than permanent for two
	  reasons: continuous connectable advertising is a measurable power line
	  item on a five-year primary cell, and an always-on BLE interface that can
	  reflash a device controlling a water main is attack surface sitting in a
	  basement for a decade.

config APP_WORKQ_STACK_SIZE
	int "Application work queue stack size"
	default 3072
	help
	  The application work queue runs the blocking lorawan_send(), which is why
	  it is separate from the system work queue that the BLE host and the
	  settings subsystem share.

config APP_JOIN_BACKOFF_MIN_S
	int "Initial OTAA join retry backoff, seconds"
	default 30
	range 10 600

config APP_JOIN_BACKOFF_MAX_S
	int "Maximum OTAA join retry backoff, seconds"
	default 3600
	range 60 86400
	help
	  US915 join against a gateway serving one sub-band is routinely slow,
	  because the device sweeps 72 channels and only 8 are listened to. Backing
	  off to an hour is a battery decision, not a politeness one.

config APP_WDT_TIMEOUT_MS
	int "Task watchdog timeout, milliseconds"
	default 300000
	help
	  Must comfortably exceed APP_SAMPLE_PERIOD_S, since the sample work
	  handler is what feeds it. Default is 5 minutes against a 60 s sample.

config APP_BATT_DIVIDER_NUM
	int "Battery divider ratio numerator"
	default 1
	help
	  Measured battery voltage is (adc_mv * NUM) / DEN. Both default to 1,
	  i.e. no divider, because the correct values are a property of the
	  specific carrier board's resistors and MUST be taken from its schematic
	  and then checked against a meter. A wrong ratio here does not fail
	  loudly; it silently mis-reports the battery column that 08-roadmap.md
	  §8 risk 4 uses as a leading indicator.

config APP_BATT_DIVIDER_DEN
	int "Battery divider ratio denominator"
	default 1
	range 1 1000

menu "LoRaWAN join credentials (bench bring-up only)"

config APP_DEV_EUI
	string "DevEUI, 16 hex characters"
	default ""
	help
	  Bench fallback only, and empty by default on purpose: a device with no
	  credentials refuses to join and logs why, rather than shipping with a
	  default key. Production credentials are written per device to the
	  settings partition at manufacture or over BLE at commissioning. A fleet
	  sharing one AppKey is a fleet with one compromise.

config APP_JOIN_EUI
	string "JoinEUI/AppEUI, 16 hex characters"
	default ""

config APP_APP_KEY
	string "AppKey, 32 hex characters"
	default ""
	help
	  Never commit a real key to this repository.

endmenu

menu "Shutoff valve"

config APP_VALVE_PRESENT
	bool "Valve hardware is fitted"
	default n
	help
	  Off by default because the year-1 SKU is sensor-only: 08-roadmap.md §10,
	  "No inline valve in year 1. Triggers every gate at once; resell a
	  certified one." With this off, the valve state machine is still built and
	  still instantiated — with a NULL hardware backend, so every request
	  answers VALVE_RC_NO_HW. That is deliberate: compiling the state machine
	  out would let the shipped build diverge from the tested one.

	  Requires valve-close-gpios and valve-open-gpios on the zephyr,user node.

config APP_LOCAL_SHUTOFF_ENABLED
	bool "Allow the local detector to close the valve"
	default n
	depends on APP_VALVE_PRESENT
	help
	  SHADOW MODE IS THE DEFAULT AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL. Standing rule 3,
	  08-roadmap.md §0: no customer-visible action until the nuisance rate is
	  measured. An insurer's trust is spent once.

	  With this off, the detector still runs, still produces verdicts, still
	  logs them and still uplinks them — nothing actuates. That is what shadow
	  mode means on the device side, and it is the mirror of the backend's
	  alerting_enabled=false / status="shadow" behaviour in
	  contracts/INTERFACES.md §8.

	  Turning this on is a product decision gated on the P1 exit criterion,
	  not a configuration preference.

config APP_VALVE_PULSE_MS
	int "Latching solenoid drive pulse, milliseconds"
	default 250
	range 20 2000
	depends on APP_VALVE_PRESENT
	help
	  A latching solenoid needs one full pulse and then holds position with no
	  current, which is what makes it inherently fail-as-is
	  (05-open-source-stack.md §5.3). Take the real figure from the valve
	  datasheet; too short is a half-latched stem.

config APP_VALVE_TORQUE_REFUSE_MNM
	int "Breakaway torque above which we refuse to arm, mN.m"
	default 4000
	range 100 50000
	help
	  TORQUE_REFUSE_THRESHOLD in 05-open-source-stack.md §5.3. THE DEFAULT IS
	  NOT A MEASURED NUMBER — it is the right order of magnitude for a 3/4"
	  quarter-turn ball valve and nothing more. Replace it with a bench torque
	  wrench figure for the specific valve and actuator, correlated against the
	  current-sense proxy the firmware actually measures.

	  08-roadmap.md §8 risk 9's leading indicator is "any unit arming above the
	  breakaway-torque threshold", so this number is the metric.

config APP_VALVE_CYCLE_TIMEOUT_MS
	int "Full-travel cycle timeout, milliseconds"
	default 8000
	range 100 60000
	help
	  CYCLE_TIMEOUT_MS in 05-open-source-stack.md §5.3. An overrun is a
	  mechanical problem, so it produces V_FAULT rather than V_REFUSED, and
	  V_FAULT is sticky until a human clears it.

config APP_VALVE_MIN_ACTUATE_MV
	int "Minimum battery to permit a CLOSE, millivolts"
	default 3000
	range 1800 4200
	help
	  Below this the state machine refuses to close but still permits an open.
	  The asymmetry is the point: a failed open leaves the valve where it was,
	  while a failed close risks a partially driven stem — a new failure mode —
	  and closed is never the safe default. See the invariants in src/valve.h.

endmenu

module = APP
module-str = app
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
